tation and Solar Panel Bundle is available for $309.99, discounted 23% from its $399.99 regular price. Designed for emergencies, travel, and off-grid use, the power station can charge up to eight devices simultaneously through three DC ports, two AC outlets, and three USB ports, including USB-C and quick-charging options. Its 93,120mAh/298Wh battery uses a pure sine wave inverter for stable power and includes an LED flashlight and digital battery display. The unit can be recharged through a wall outlet, car charger, or the included waterproof folding solar panel. The panel converts approximately 21%\u201323% of sunlight into usable energy, can charge devices directly, and includes 10 connector plugs for broad compatibility. The compact, lightweight design makes the bundle convenient for outdoor activities and emergency preparedness. The promotional price is subject to change and availability.","ref_id":{"turn_index":951235,"ref_type":"news","ref_index":15},"pub_date":1747762211.0,"attribution":"www.sfgate.com"}]},{"type":"search_result_group","domain":"www.digitalcameraworld.com","entries":[{"type":"search_result","url":"https://www.digitalcameraworld.com/buying-guides/best-laptop-power-bank","title":"The best portable power banks and power stations in 2026: stay topped up, on the go, or in the event of a power outage","snippet":"This guide recommends four portable power options for keeping laptops and other devices charged while traveling, working off-grid, or during outages. The DJI Power 1000 is a 1,024Wh, 2,200W power station aimed especially at drone users, with fast USB-C and DJI-specific charging ports, though it lacks app features and is relatively heavy. The UGREEN 300W 48,000mAh is the best overall laptop power bank, charging up to five devices and offering high capacity, but weighs 1.86kg and does not include a charging plug. For fast charging, the UGREEN 145W provides 25,000mAh and a 100W USB-C port in a 505g package, though its power-output options can be confusing. The Anker Prime 20,000mAh offers up to 200W total output and a particularly useful display showing charge levels and time remaining. The guide advises choosing at least 20,000mAh for laptop use and checking that the bank\u2019s ports and cables match the laptop.","ref_id":{"turn_index":951235,"ref_type":"news","ref_index":12},"pub_date":1793118795.0,"thumbnail_url":"https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-1/AGX8l43xoy-69LY4WVGAantB4WcJVCU3k3jdvLiTmRmdSoAyHdGNKBI7KFJ0RG18DNTwWpje7F8EihYh9RjD2qacsoNnwlt81EBFOoxHZo2UyG5DJganoS61s6tnAih4","attribution":"www.digitalcameraworld.com"}]},{"type":"search_result_group","domain":"nymag.com","entries":[{"type":"search_result","url":"https://nymag.com/strategist/article/best-emergency-kit-items.html?utm_campaign=feed-part&utm_medium=social_acct&utm_source=rss","title":"The Best Items to Stock for Any Emergency, According to Survivalists","snippet":"The article compiles emergency-preparedness advice from government agencies and 22 survivalists, preppers, and emergency professionals. Its central message is to prepare for peace of mind, keep supplies practical and manageable, and understand personal limits rather than overloading a go-bag. Core recommendations include a backpack or other portable storage; flashlight or headlamp; multi-tool; customized first-aid kit and a month of essential medicines; hand-crank radio; fire-starting tools; rechargeable batteries and power bank; warm bedding; hygiene and cleaning supplies; and familiar, nonperishable food. Store at least one gallon of water per person per day for seven days, plus containers and ways to purify more. Additional gear may include masks, gloves, goggles, emergency blankets, whistle, tarp, duct tape, paracord, cooking equipment, and a tent. Experts stress having a written, practiced household plan, keeping supplies accessible, testing equipment, and protecting important documents. The article also suggests optional items such as a generator, fuel, solar chargers, maps, and Faraday bags. Choose supplies suited to likely hazards, household needs, and the ability to carry or use them.","ref_id":{"turn_index":951235,"ref_type":"news","ref_index":13},"pub_date":1793193780.0,"thumbnail_url":"https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-1/9u0iDux4dq7bRHzwqJC6mqkybSJTM-8lui525dcoKP6q4I0NemCGz_YwjZAyKKlaL9XiE7P87iCZ0w3wpQoV4n67548yDG_z7ZkcxiAzp9XahJlcySZFsCotworde8zC7UGRT_4F_elFRBDnz7jWq5MOKsOZwdyAqKIe8VlLDXQ","attribution":"nymag.com"},{"type":"search_result","url":"https://nymag.com/strategist/article/best-emergency-preparedness-items-for-first-time-homeowners.html?utm_campaign=feed-part&utm_medium=social_acct&utm_source=rss","title":"The Emergency-Preparedness Items I'm Buying As a First-Time Homeowner","snippet":"This guide helps first-time homeowners prepare for fires, floods, storms, power outages, evacuations, and other emergencies. Experts recommend maintaining both a portable go bag and a two-week stay-at-home supply kit containing one gallon of water per person per day, nonperishable food, lighting, a radio, first-aid supplies, medications, sanitation items, important documents, and cash. Suggested household equipment includes fire extinguishers and fire blankets, water-leak sensors, a wet/dry vacuum, flood barriers, emergency radios, portable chargers or power stations, lanterns, headlamps, and a properly ventilated generator with carbon-monoxide protection. Evacuation kits should also include N95 masks, prescription medicines, customizable first-aid supplies, and pet necessities such as food, water, leashes, carriers, bowls, and identification photos. For more severe disruptions, the article recommends trauma kits, portable toilets, camping stoves, and water filters or purifiers. Rechargeable devices should carry certification from an OSHA-recognized Nationally Recognized Testing Laboratory because of lithium-ion battery risks. Homeowners should also enable Wireless Emergency Alerts on their phones.","ref_id":{"turn_index":9512